{
  "title": "Refresh and resend",
  "idea": "Two controllers reissue credentials: `refreshAccessToken` trades a valid refresh token for a new pair, and `resendEmailVerification` replaces an old verification link.",
  "analogy": {
    "text": "A hotel key card that stops working each day. At the desk you show your booking slip and get a new card and slip; the old slip is voided.",
    "breaks": "The desk sees your face; the server sees only the token."
  },
  "points": [
    "`refreshAccessToken` verifies the refresh token, then checks it equals the stored one.",
    "On a match it signs a new pair and stores the new refresh token.",
    "That is rotation: a used or revoked refresh token fails the comparison with `401`.",
    "`resendEmailVerification` stores a new hash and expiry, and mails the new raw token."
  ],
  "hero": {
